.TH STUDIO-BRIGHTNESS 1 "October 2026" "studio-brightness 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
studio-brightness, studio-brightness-gui, studio-brightness-osd \- Studio Brightness, brightness control for Apple displays
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B studio-brightness
.RB [ \-d
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-osd | \-\-notify ]
.BR list | get | set | up | down
.RI [ VALUE ]
.br
.B studio-brightness-gui
.br
.B studio-brightness-osd
.I PERCENT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B studio-brightness
gets and sets the brightness of Apple Cinema, Thunderbolt and Studio Displays and the
Pro Display XDR. These displays have no DDC/CI; brightness is sent over the display's
USB cable, which must be connected to the computer.
.PP
Displays known to the kernel
.B appledisplay
driver are controlled through
.IR /sys/class/backlight/appledisplay* ;
all others through HID feature reports on
.IR /dev/hidraw* .
.PP
.B studio-brightness-gui
opens a window with one brightness slider per display.
.B studio-brightness-osd
shows an on-screen brightness indicator for a moment; it is what
.B \-\-osd
runs.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Show detected displays and which backend each uses.
.TP
.BR get " [" \-\-raw ]
Print the brightness in percent, or the raw hardware value.
.TP
.BI set " VALUE"
Set the brightness. Accepts 60, 60%, +10 or \-10.
.TP
.BR up " [" \fISTEP\fR "], " down " [" \fISTEP\fR ]
Change the brightness by STEP percent, 10 by default.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " NAME" "\fR, \fB\-\-display " NAME
Act only on this display, as named by
.BR list .
May be repeated. Without it, every command applies to all displays.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-osd
Show the on-screen indicator with the new brightness.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-notify
Show a desktop notification with the new brightness.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-studio-brightness.rules
Gives the logged-in user access to the displays and hands Cinema Displays from
usbhid to the appledisplay driver.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if no display was found or a display could not be controlled.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/mfat/studio-brightness-linux
